From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MX84 bring-up <mx84@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:15:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: gpio-ich: enable the MX84 LED GPIO on request

Coreboot leaves the MX84's SUS GPIO3 in native-function mode, while the
factory board setup expects GPIO offset 35 to control the LP5562 reset line.
Switch that one pin to GPIO mode when the DMI-gated MX84 board driver requests
it.  Other pins and systems retain the generic driver's firmware-owned muxing.
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-ich.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-ich.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-ich.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-ich.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-ich.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
+#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/driver.h>
 #include <linux/ioport.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/lpc_ich.h>
@@ -221,11 +222,24 @@ static int ichx_gpio_get(struct gpio_chip *chip, unsigned int nr)
 	}
 }
 
+static const struct dmi_system_id mx84_dmi_table[] = {
+	{
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Cisco Meraki"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "MX84-HW"),
+		},
+	},
+	{}
+};
+
 static int ichx_gpio_request(struct gpio_chip *chip, unsigned int nr)
 {
 	if (!ichx_gpio_check_available(chip, nr))
 		return -ENXIO;
 
+	if (nr == 35 && dmi_check_system(mx84_dmi_table))
+		ichx_write_bit(GPIO_USE_SEL, nr, 1, 0);
+
 	/*
 	 * Note we assume the BIOS properly set a bridge's USE value.  Some
 	 * chips (eg Intel 3100) have bogus USE values though, so first see if
